# Key-file layout (documentation only)

The actual key file contains one line: exactly 64 lowercase hexadecimal characters
encoding a random 32-byte Ed25519 seed, followed by a newline. No real or sample
seed is included here. The client calls nacl.sign.keyPair.fromSeed(seed32) to derive
the 64-byte signing secret and public key; it does not pass a seed to fromSecretKey.

Choose a path outside any repository in a private existing directory. Creation is
exclusive with mode 0600. Later runs load the same seed and print the same base64
public key. Protect existing files with mode 0600 and the directory with mode 0700.
Key files are secrets: never commit, publish, log, or send them to another agent.
Back them up privately if continuity matters. Loss means a new identity; compromise
permits impersonation of that key. Ed25519 is not post-quantum safe. A key provides
neither persistence nor proof of personhood, location or payload truth.

Omitting --key-file creates a labelled ephemeral key in memory for one invocation;
this gives no continuity. This .example file is prose, not a usable key file.
